   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the economic development law, in relation to developing a senior tourism program",
    "basePrintNo": "S6694",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6694-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Art 5-F §§181-f - 181-g, Ec Dev L",
    "lawSection": "Economic Development Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6694\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the economic development law, in\nrelation to developing a senior tourism program\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo create a \"New York Senior Tourism\" program\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\n§ 1 amends the economic development law by adding a new article 5-f\nwhich creates a \"New York Senior Tourism\" program, identifies the\nlegislative intent, defines terms for the program and outlines the\nguidelines for its implementation.\n\n§ 2 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nNew York State has experienced record tourism numbers in recent years.\n2016 had a record 239 million visitors to the state, which generated\n$104.8 billion in economic activity; the third year in a row that\nnumber has topped one billion. Tourism is the state's fourth largest\nindustry, employing 914,000 New Yorkers. New York ranks third in the\nnation for the number of seniors with over 3.7 million individuals\nover the age of 60. Trends indicate that the state's population will\ncontinue to age, following nationwide trends.\n\nIn 2009, the Spanish government created the successful \"Europe Senior\nTourism\" program. The program was designed to increase tourism to the\ncountry of Spain during the off season and has drawn more than 150,000\npeople to the country since its creation.\n\nThis legislation will create a \"New York Senior Tourism\" program,\nsimilar to the.I Love NY LGBT targeted tourism initiative The creation\nof this initiative will allow the state to take advantage of its\ngrowing tourism industry and increased senior population. A senior\ntourism program will not only keep and bring in increased tourism\ndollars to the state, but it will encourage our senior population to\nage actively and stylishly in the state.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nMinimal.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThe act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
